---
pagination:
  data: iocIndex.indicator_browse_pages
  size: 1
  alias: run
permalink: "{{ run.url }}"
layout: base.njk
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
eleventyComputed:
  title: "{{ run.kind.plural | safe }}{% if run.of > 1 %}, page {{ run.number | safe }} of {{ run.of | safe }}{% endif %}"
  head_title: "{{ run.kind.plural | safe }} in DPRK threat reporting{% if run.of > 1 %}, page {{ run.number | safe }} of {{ run.of | safe }}{% endif %}"
  description: "{{ run.kind.plural | safe }} reported in published sources on North Korean (DPRK) cyber operations{% if run.of > 1 %}, {{ run.first | safe }} to {{ run.last | safe }} (page {{ run.number | safe }} of {{ run.of | safe }}){% endif %}. Each links to its own page with every citation."
---
{#
  src/indicators/browse.njk — a rendered link to every /indicators/{id}/ page

  The searches on /remote-workers/ and the cluster pages build their results
  in the browser from a downloaded index, so nothing in the built HTML linked
  to most indicator pages: a search engine knew them only from the sitemap,
  and a page with no link pointing at it is the one it fetches last, if at
  all. These pages exist to give each indicator page an ordinary link whose
  anchor text is the value itself. They are also the only way through the
  full set without JavaScript.

  One run of pages per indicator type, at /indicators/browse/{type}/ and
  /indicators/browse/{type}/{n}/, so a page holds one kind of value and says
  so in its title. The runs are cut in src/_data/iocIndex.js (browseRuns), and
  /indicators/ and /indicators/browse/ both link to every one of them, which
  keeps any indicator page three clicks from the home page.

  The rows link to /indicators/{id}/ even for a value that also sits on a
  persona page, rather than using partials/ioc-result.njk, whose rows go to
  the persona page: this listing exists to reach the indicator pages.
#}
<section>
  {% set backLink = { url: "/indicators/browse/", text: "Browse indicators" } %}{% include "partials/back-link.njk" %}
  <h1>{{ run.kind.plural }}</h1>
  <p>
    {{ run.total | thousands }} {% if run.total == 1 %}{{ run.kind.label }}{% else %}{{ run.kind.plural_text }}{% endif %}
    reported in published sources on North Korean (DPRK) cyber operations,
    ordered by value{% if run.of > 1 %}, {{ run.records.length }} to a page. This
    is page {{ run.number }} of {{ run.of }}, from <code>{{ run.first }}</code>
    to <code>{{ run.last }}</code>{% endif %}. Each value links to its own page,
    which carries every source that reported it and the text around it. Other
    types are listed in the <a href="/indicators/browse/">browse directory</a>.
  </p>
  {% if run.of > 1 %}
  <nav class="pagination" aria-label="{{ run.kind.plural }} pages, before the table">
    {% if run.prev %}<a class="btn btn--secondary" href="{{ run.prev }}" rel="prev">&larr; Previous</a>{% endif %}
    <span>Page {{ run.number }} of {{ run.of }}</span>
    {% if run.next %}<a class="btn btn--secondary" href="{{ run.next }}" rel="next">Next &rarr;</a>{% endif %}
  </nav>
  {% endif %}
  <div class="table-scroll">
    <table class="results-table">
      <thead>
        <tr><th scope="col">Value</th><th scope="col">Campaign</th><th scope="col">Filed under</th><th scope="col">Sources</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {% for record in run.records %}
        <tr>
          <td><a href="/indicators/{{ record.id }}/"><code>{{ record | iocLabel }}</code></a></td>
          <td>{% for campaign in record.campaign %}<span class="tag-chip">{{ campaign }}</span>{% endfor %}</td>
          <td>{% for owner in record.personas %}<a href="/remote-workers/personas/{{ owner.slug }}/">{{ owner.name | default(owner.slug) }}</a>{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}</td>
          <td>{{ record.sources.length }}</td>
        </tr>
        {% endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  {% if run.of > 1 %}
  <nav class="pagination" aria-label="{{ run.kind.plural }} pages, after the table">
    {% if run.prev %}<a class="btn btn--secondary" href="{{ run.prev }}" rel="prev">&larr; Previous</a>{% endif %}
    <span>Page {{ run.number }} of {{ run.of }}</span>
    {% if run.next %}<a class="btn btn--secondary" href="{{ run.next }}" rel="next">Next &rarr;</a>{% endif %}
  </nav>
  {% endif %}
</section>
<section>
  {% set disclaimer = {
    title: "Disclaimer",
    preset: "not-proof",
    body: 'Compromised packages and repositories name victims. See the <a href="/sources/#sourcing-methodology">sourcing methodology</a>.'
  } %}{% include "partials/disclaimer.njk" %}
</section>
